From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: present into a window another process owns

On Windows any process may create a swapchain on another process's window,
and Chromium relies on it: without DirectComposition (a stub in Wine), its
GPU process presents into the browser process's compositor window. The PS5
window surface was bound only when the presenter owned the window, so
a launcher's sign-in window could not be shown (2026-10-10, record removed from the tree; in git history:
VK_ERROR_SURFACE_LOST_KHR, then CreateSwapChainForHwnd failed).

The surface is now bound to any window that has an owning process; the
broker files the frames under that owner, and drops them when the
presenter exits (src/pw_window_scene.h). A refusal is logged with the
window, its owner, the presenter and the generation.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
index c6ee725..1eac766 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -971,14 +971,21 @@ static VkResult ps5_vulkan_surface_create( HWND hwnd, BOOL raw, const struct vul
     if (res == VK_SUCCESS && window_surfaces)
     {
         UINT64 generation=0;
+        int owner=0,bound=-1;
+        /* Any process may present into a window another owns, as on Windows: Chromium's GPU process presents
+         * into the browser process's compositor window when DirectComposition is unavailable. The broker files the
+         * frames under the window's owner (src/pw_window_scene.h); only a window with no owning process is refused. */
         SERVER_START_REQ(get_window_info)
         {
             req->handle=wine_server_user_handle(hwnd);
-            if(!wine_server_call(req) && reply->native_pid==getpid())generation=reply->generation;
+            if(!wine_server_call(req) && reply->native_pid>0) {owner=reply->native_pid;generation=reply->generation;}
         }
         SERVER_END_REQ;
-        if(!generation || !bind_gpu_window || bind_gpu_window(*handle,(UINT)(UINT_PTR)hwnd,generation))
+        if(generation && bind_gpu_window)bound=bind_gpu_window(*handle,(UINT)(UINT_PTR)hwnd,generation);
+        if(bound)
         {
+            ERR("window surface refused: hwnd %p owner %d presenter %d generation %s bind %d\n",hwnd,owner,
+                (int)getpid(),wine_dbgstr_longlong(generation),bound);
             instance->p_vkDestroySurfaceKHR(instance->host.instance,*handle,NULL);
             *handle=VK_NULL_HANDLE;
             res=VK_ERROR_SURFACE_LOST_KHR;
